<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Articles of Union (1964)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Articles of the Union between Tanganyika and Zanzibar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Articles of Union were the agreement signed on 22 April 1964 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a> of Tanganyika and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abeid-karume">Abeid Karume</a> of Zanzibar, uniting the two states as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-republic-of-tanganyika-and-zanzibar">United Republic of Tanganyika and Zanzibar</a> from 26 April 1964, renamed Tanzania later that year. They reserved certain matters to the union government while Zanzibar kept its own government for other affairs, an arrangement that remains a source of political tension.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…to contain the instability of the islands and the competition of Cold War powers there, Nyerere and Karume signed the <b>Articles of Union</b>, and on 26 April 1964 the United Republic of Tanganyika and Zanzibar came into being, renamed the United Republic of Tanzania on 29 October 1964.</blockquote><a href="/empire/tanzania">Tanzania · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
